/T (the most frequently misunderstood topics in Object-Oriented Programming is the object lifecycle: the exact sequence in which constructors and destructors execute when inheritance, composition and polymorphism are involved. Students regularly lose marks in examinations and interviews because they cannot predict this order correctly.)
/E (the most frequently misunderstood topics in Object-Oriented Programming is the object lifecycle: the exact sequence in which constructors and destructors execute when inheritance, composition and polymorphism are involved. Students regularly lose marks in examinations and interviews because they cannot predict this order correctly.)
