131 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 66 0 R
/T (The Constructor's Dilemma is a text-based C++ game in which the player reads a short C++ program and predicts the exact output produced by constructor and destructor calls. After each answer, the game presents a step-by-step Lifecycle Trace that reveals the correct order with a one-line explanation for each step. The project is built entirely in standard C++ using inheritance, polymorphism, composition, encapsulation and file I/O, without external libraries. It covers five concept areas: constructor order, destructor order, composition, virtual destructors, and copy/assignment semantics.)
/E (The Constructor's Dilemma is a text-based C++ game in which the player reads a short C++ program and predicts the exact output produced by constructor and destructor calls. After each answer, the game presents a step-by-step Lifecycle Trace that reveals the correct order with a one-line explanation for each step. The project is built entirely in standard C++ using inheritance, polymorphism, composition, encapsulation and file I/O, without external libraries. It covers five concept areas: constructor order, destructor order, composition, virtual destructors, and copy/assignment semantics.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [22]
>>
