/Title (The Constructor's Dilemma demonstrates that a college project can be simultaneously simple to build, rich in OOP concepts and genuinely useful. By targeting a specific, well-known weakness in how students learn C++ - object lifecycle order - the project turns a passive revision topic into an interactive challenge.)
/Dest [21 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 561 0 R
/Next 685 0 R
>>
endobj
685 0 obj
<<
/Title (The use of inheritance, polymorphism, composition, encapsulation and file handling mirrors what is taught in the classroom, while the Lifecycle Trace adds an original educational dimension that no standard quiz provides. The project is lightweight, portable and extensible, and can be used directly by students preparing for examinations and interviews. Above all, it proves a simple idea: the best way to understand code is to see exactly what it does, step by step.)
/Dest [21 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 561 0 R
/Prev 684 0 R
>>
endobj
