/Title (the most frequently misunderstood topics in Object-Oriented Programming is the object lifecycle: the exact sequence in which constructors and destructors execute when inheritance, composition and polymorphism are involved. Students regularly lose marks in examinations and interviews because they cannot predict this order correctly.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 775 0 R
/Prev 846 0 R
/Next 921 0 R
>>
endobj
921 0 obj
<<
/Title (The Constructor's Dilemma is a text-based C++ game in which the player reads a short C++ program and predicts the exact output produced by constructor and destructor calls. After each answer, the game presents a step-by-step Lifecycle Trace that reveals the correct order with a one-line explanation for each step. The project is built entirely in standard C++ using inheritance, polymorphism, composition, encapsulation and file I/O, without external libraries. It covers five concept areas: constructor order, destructor order, composition, virtual destructors, and copy/assignment semantics.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 775 0 R
/Prev 920 0 R
/Next 847 0 R
>>
endobj
